---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';

// Keep the in-app paths in these answers in sync with the real app.
const email = '[SUPPORT EMAIL]';
---

<Base page="support" title="Where's My Crown? – Support" description="Help and answers for Where's My Crown?">
  <section class="night">
    <div class="container narrow hero">
      <h1 class="title">SUPPORT</h1>
      <p>Stuck in the maze, or something not working as it should? Start with the answers below, or write to us.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="contact-h">
    <div class="container narrow contact-wrap">
      <div class="contact">
        <div class="contact-copy">
          <h2 id="contact-h" class="ui">Contact us</h2>
          <p>
            Email us and a real person will reply. If you're reporting a problem, please tell us your device
            (for example iPad 10th generation) and iOS version.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a href={`mailto:${email}`} class="pixel email">{email}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="faq-h">
    <div class="container narrow faq">
      <h2 id="faq-h" class="section-title">Common questions</h2>

      <Faq q="How do you play?">
        <p>
          Help the princess walk through the maze to her crown. Tap any spot on the path and she walks there by
          herself, or use the big arrow buttons, or swipe. Watch out for the dragon: if it catches her, she loses a
          heart and hops back to a safe spot. Finding the crown unlocks the next maze.
        </p>
      </Faq>

      <Faq q="What are helpers?">
        <p>
          Before each maze you can bring a helper. The unicorn chases the dragon away (and can be ridden), the fairy
          puts it to sleep, and the owl shows the way to the crown. In the free version a helper costs one short ad;
          with the Royal Pass every helper is free.
        </p>
      </Faq>

      <Faq q="Why is there a maths question?">
        <p>
          That's the grown-up gate. Purchases and settings are behind a quick multiplication question so little ones
          can't buy anything or change settings by accident.
        </p>
      </Faq>

      <Faq q="I bought the Royal Pass. How do I restore it on a new device?">
        <p>
          Sign in with the same Apple Account you used to buy it. Then on the title screen tap
          <strong>For grown-ups</strong>, answer the question, open <strong>Royal Pass</strong> and tap
          <strong>Restore purchase</strong>.
        </p>
      </Faq>

      <Faq q="How do I get a refund?">
        <p>
          Purchases are handled by Apple, so refunds are too. You can request one at
          <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>. If something went wrong with your
          purchase, email us as well and we'll help.
        </p>
      </Faq>

      <Faq q="How do I turn off the sound or the reading voice?">
        <p>
          On the title screen tap <strong>For grown-ups</strong>, answer the question, then switch
          <strong>Sound</strong> or <strong>Read aloud</strong> off.
        </p>
      </Faq>

      <Faq q="How do I start the mazes over?">
        <p>
          Tap <strong>For grown-ups</strong> on the title screen, answer the question and choose
          <strong>Reset maze progress</strong>. All mazes except the first one lock again. Your Royal Pass and
          dress-up choices are kept.
        </p>
      </Faq>

      <Faq q="It's a bit too hard for my child. Any tips?">
        <p>
          Try bringing the fairy or the unicorn: both deal with the dragon so the maze becomes a calm walk. The owl is
          great for children who get lost, because it draws arrows all the way to the crown.
        </p>
      </Faq>

      <p class="after">Looking for how we handle data? Read our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding-top: 56px;
    padding-bottom: 64px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(26px, 4vw, 40px); line-height: 1.3; }
  .hero p { font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--on-night-lead); max-width: 40rem; }

  .contact-wrap { padding-top: 48px; }
  .contact {
    background: var(--card);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px var(--ink), 8px 8px 0 4px var(--gold);
    padding: 28px;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 20px;
  }
  .contact-copy {
    flex: 1 1 360px;
    min-width: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .contact h2 { font-size: 28px; }
  .contact p { font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.55; }
  .email {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 52px;
    padding: 0 24px;
    background: var(--gold);
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.4;
    box-shadow: inset -4px -4px 0 var(--gold-deep), 0 0 0 4px var(--ink);
  }
  .email:hover { color: var(--ink); }

  .faq {
    padding-top: 56px;
    padding-bottom: 80px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  .faq h2 { font-size: clamp(18px, 2.4vw, 24px); margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .after { margin-top: 16px; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; }
</style>
